---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Privacy - devreads.fyi" description="How devreads.fyi handles local preferences, optional account sync, page-view counts, cookie consent, and analytics.">
  <div class="page-head">
    <h1 style="font-family: var(--mono);">$ cat privacy</h1>
    <p>Short version: optional account sync for favorites, a shared page-view count, and analytics cookie choices managed by CookieHub.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="max-width: 560px; font-size: 14px; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.7;">
    <p style="font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 13px; color: var(--faint);">// what stays on your device</p>
    <p>Your theme choice and read marker stay in your browser's localStorage. Favorites are also saved locally when you're not signed in. Clearing site data removes local favorites and preferences.</p>
    <p style="font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 13px; color: var(--faint);">// optional accounts and favorites</p>
    <p>If you sign in with Google, GitHub or LinkedIn, the site stores your provider identity, name, email when supplied, and favorites in Cloudflare D1. Signing in automatically merges favorites saved in this browser into your account, so you can read them on other devices. We request basic identity information, not access to your repositories, contacts or social posts.</p>
    <p>Necessary authentication cookies keep you signed in for up to 30 days, renewed when you use your account. They are separate from analytics consent. Sign-out clears the browser's account state; synchronized favorites remain in your account. You can delete your account and its cloud favorites from the Account page after a recent sign-in. Session IP addresses and user-agent strings are not retained in the application database; Cloudflare still processes request information to serve the site and apply rate limits.</p>
    <p style="font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 13px; color: var(--faint);">// cookie choices</p>
    <p><a href="https://www.cookiehub.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="text-decoration: underline;">CookieHub</a> manages cookie consent and remembers your choices in a necessary consent cookie. You can review or change those choices using <a href="#" class="ch2-open-settings-btn" style="text-decoration: underline;">cookie settings</a> here or in the footer. CookieHub processes consent records and technical information needed to provide this service.</p>
    <p style="font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 13px; color: var(--faint);">// shared page-view counter</p>
    <p>The footer shows a cumulative count of page views, including reloads, recorded by the site's Cloudflare Worker. Its starting total includes historical aggregate page views from Cloudflare analytics. The counter stores aggregate counts: no cookies, IP addresses or visitor identifiers. It does not identify unique people or track you across pages. Live updates use a same-origin WebSocket connection.</p>
    <p style="font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 13px; color: var(--faint);">// usage analytics</p>
    <p>The site uses <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="text-decoration: underline;">Google Analytics 4</a> to measure page views and site usage, including referrers and browser and device information. CookieHub controls Google's consent signals. Analytics cookies and storage depend on your consent choices and the configured regional settings.</p>
    <p>Google Consent Mode is currently configured in advanced mode. Google may receive limited cookieless measurement requests before analytics consent is granted. Changing your cookie settings updates the signals used for future measurements.</p>
    <p style="font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 13px; color: var(--faint);">// what third parties see</p>
    <p>The site is served by Cloudflare, which processes standard request logs (such as IP addresses) to deliver pages and protect against abuse. Post thumbnails load directly from each publisher's servers, so those servers see your IP address when an image loads; the referrer is suppressed. When you open a post or use its share button, the publisher's link carries a <code>utm_source=devreads.fyi</code> parameter so publishers can see that this site sent them a reader. Copied links and social shares include the same attribution. It identifies the site, not you.</p>
    <p style="font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 13px; color: var(--faint);">// if this ever changes</p>
    <p>If the site ever adds ads or a newsletter, this page will describe exactly what that involves before it happens. Questions or concerns: email <a data-u="contact" data-d="devreads.fyi" style="text-decoration: underline; cursor: pointer;">contact [at] devreads [dot] fyi</a> or open an issue on <a href="https://github.com/iamsunny/devreads.fyi" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="text-decoration: underline;">GitHub</a>.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
